{Hardware::VehicleIssue::Feedback::SlowVehicle
Hi Vojtech,

Thanks for reaching out!

In many cases, the reason that the vehicle may slow down is if you're in a slow zone. Slow zones are represented in yellow in the map and as you enter the vehicle will begin to reduce its speed.

Slow zones are placed in areas that are usually crowded with either cars or pedestrians. So, the vehicle will automatically slow down a bit here for the safety of you and others.

I recommend checking your route in the app before you ride so you can be aware if you'll be entering any slow zones along the way.

If you have any further questions, please let me know.}

{Hardware::VehicleIssue::ShutDownDuringRide::Battery
Hi Vojtech,

Thanks for reaching out.

If the vehicle unexpectedly slowed down or stopped during your ride, it was probably because it ran out of battery.

You can always see the vehicle's battery level in the app by tapping the vehicle’s icon on the map. Once you’ve unlocked a vehicle, you can also see the battery level on the handlebar screen. If the battery light is green, the vehicle is well charged; yellow light means the battery will last for another – short – ride; red light means the vehicle needs charging.

Another possible reason why the vehicle went slower is that you entered a slow-speed or no-riding zone. Check the in-app map to see if you’re in one of these zones.

Please reach out again if you have more questions.

Best,}

{Hardware::VehicleIssue::ShutDownDuringRide::NoRidingZone
